diagnostics/nested-function-captures.em:36:15: this is String?, so `upper` may not be there to use
          print(note.upper())
                ^^^^
A test cannot prove `note` is there, because a block or a nested function can set it back to `nothing` at any time. Copy it into a `const` and test that, or give it a fallback with `.or(...)`.
